      "content": "Of course that thought crosses your mind — when pain becomes the loudest thing in your life, \"stopping\" starts to sound like relief. But what you're describing isn't rationality; it's exhaustion wearing a mask of logic. You're not looking at the facts — you're looking at a fogged mirror. Give up on *everything* for good, and you'd also be ending the possibility of ever feeling differently, of ever finding a version of life that doesn't weigh this much. You don't need to find the point where it's \"okay\" — you need to find a single person or a single moment that can hold you until the fog lifts.",
